description:
FILED s539a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-13).

Reproducer (scratch/s539a/pr2/dn1.pl):
  use Test::More tests => 1;
  diag "line one\n";
  note "note one\n";
  diag "two\nlines\n";
  ok(1);
perl prints `# line one` / `# note one` / `# two` / `# lines`; PCL (main 24988e35 and s539a) prints an extra `# ` line after each message that ends in a newline (Test::Builder strips ONE trailing newline before splitting into `# ` lines; it also skips an empty message).  Seen first through Test::Warnings' `allow_warnings` (pr/tw2.pl: `# allowed` then `# `).  Cosmetic in TAP (a comment line) but visible on STDOUT for `note`.  Fix in cl/pcl-test.lisp's diag/note formatter; guard in Pl/t/tap-assert-01.t.
